          },
          "worked": "Using part (a), the union has probability at most 1:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cup B\\cup C)&\\le1\\\\0.9+P(A\\cap B\\cap C)&\\le1\\\\P(A\\cap B\\cap C)&\\le0.10.\\end{align*}$$\n\nProbabilities are nonnegative, so $0\\le P(A\\cap B\\cap C)\\le0.10$. These values are feasible: the pairwise-only regions have probabilities $0.20-t$, $0.15-t$ and $0.10-t$, the three single-event regions each have probability $0.15+t$, and the outside region has probability $0.10-t$, where $t=P(A\\cap B\\cap C)$. All are nonnegative throughout this interval.",
